canvas: 3 diagrams on one canvas, drawn whole at 100%
diagram d1 "worker and runtime: the two RPC seams" at 0,3: extent=68x6 nodes=2 edges=2 routes=2
  description: modal-worker sends task input and control RPCs to modal-runtime; modal-runtime sends events and management RPCs back. Two routes, two directions, no merged arrow.
diagram d2 "task dispatch down to the container" at 0,14: extent=133x5 nodes=4 edges=3 routes=3
  description: modal-runtime dispatches tasks to the Task engine; the engine starts and manages a Container backend; that backend runs the user process inside the Task container.
diagram d3 "storage and daemon interfaces" at 0,24: extent=40x62 nodes=5 edges=3 routes=3
  description: The Task engine mounts and snapshots Filesystem + volumes, that data flows on to Blobnet, and modal-runtime reaches modal-daemon over filesystem HTTP on a Unix socket, which is not the worker gRPC seam.
